      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find out the month in which Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the frequency of the replacement**: Hal changes the batteries every 5 months.\n2. **Calculate the number of 5-month periods within 25 months**: Since he changes the batteries each 5 months, we need to find the number of full 5-month periods in 25 months.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of 5-month periods} = \\frac{25 \\text{ months}}{5 \\text{ months}} = 5 \\text{ periods}\n   \\]\n3. **Determine which month corresponds to the 5th 5-month period**: Since the 1st period starts in May, the 5th period (which is the 25th encounter) will occur 4 full cycles later (5 - 1 = 4 cycles).\n4. **Calculate the end month**: Initially, the first 5th period ends in May of the 5th year (May + 4 periods = May + 4 months). This calculation accounts for the fact that May does not have a full 6th cycle. \n\nBy adding 6 months to the start month of May (May + 6 months = Dec), we get that the 6th cycle corresponds to the 12th month (December). However, it needs to be noted that within this period, we would target another major year which falls in December, ideally just before January, the following year.\n\nThus, considering Hal being changeable 5 months sequentially would make December next the 25th round. \n\nThe month he will change the batteries for the 25th time is \\boxed{December}.",
